  "source_review": {
    "review": "The fixed22-label program performs all loop tests, strided address arithmetic, reads, products, sums and stores through literal unchanged instructions. Proof states record the actual original-memory product as an invariant; initial outputPrefix0 is exactly old memory, so no product value is supplied to the machine. Every legal trace from literal parameter registers halts with actual dense readMatrix equal to leftMatrix*rightMatrix, preserves every cell outside output, and satisfies actual CostThrough\u226417*(rows+inner+cols+1)^3. Zero rows/columns/inner are included by the universal statements and actual loop branches.",
    "hypotheses": "Only actual input entry addresses must be outside the dense output block. Zero strides and overlap between read-only input matrices are permitted. The dense nonoverlap bridge uses precisely the original DisjointBlocks definition.",
    "limits": "Matrix multiplication component started from its specified state. A whole-program input parser, global workspace layout and total algorithm cost remain separate."
  },
